From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rory Axton <roryaxton@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 23:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] 0943 redfin: display frame statistics, IOMFB modes, 90 Hz

A frame statistics line every 5 s while frames come ("SWEET FB: 5s: swaps N
shown N dropped N | le11 .. gt35 | p50 p95 ms | blitq us fence us | hz H"),
replacing the old 5 s line. Boot-arg sweetfbx=MASK (default 0 = as before):
0x1 TimingElements/ColorElements with SyncRate, GetBlock(0x40) and sel 77 =
mach_absolute_time; 0x2 no cache clean of a frame's surface unless the CPU
locked it for writing since its last present (IOSurface seed). sweetfb_hz=90
runs the S6E3HC2 at 90 Hz (DCS short write 0x53 0x38) with 11.1 ms ticks.
Poke "p fc" measures INTF1's TE frame rate over 1 s, "p hz 60|90 [tc]"
switches live. IOMFB selectors are each logged once.
